its load keeps no location)."] [518 1 "// bcFoldSafe is const_folding_safe_multiply, _power, _lshift and _mod."] [534 10 "// NB_MULTIPLY"] [549 10 "// NB_POWER"] [557 10 "// NB_LSHIFT"] [562 10 "// NB_REMAINDER"] [573 1 "// foldConstBinop is fold_const_binop."] [612 1 "// foldConstUnary is fold_const_unaryop."] [643 1 "// optimizeListsAndSets is optimize_lists_and_sets."] [688 1 "// optimizeLoadConst is basicblock_optimize_load_const."] [765 3 "// 3.15: what still loads a constant of the common ones is LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT"] [783 1 "// optimizeBasicBlock is optimize_basic_block, the constant folding of the expressions left to the compiler's flow!."] [907 1 "// bcSwaptimize is swaptimize; it returns the last index of the run."] [1024 1 "// removeUnusedConsts is remove_unused_consts."] [1099 1 "// addChecks is add_checks_for_loads_of_uninitialized_variables."] [1159 1 "// insertSuperinstructions is insert_superinstructions."] [1230 1 "// pushColdBlocksToEnd is push_cold_blocks_to_end."] [1274 1 "// handlerDepths finds each handler's start depth where its region starts (what SETUP_* did): the IR gives the depth to"] [1275 1 "// unwind to in its own stack, which is less than CPython's by the NULLs and selves of the region's start."] [1352 2 "// a handler whose region lost every instruction (try: pass) has no row: CPython's SETUP_* still sets its depth,"] [1353 2 "// the try statement's plus the exception (queue 248). Its entry follows reachable code, which ends at the try"] [1354 2 "// statement's depth"] [1358 4 "// the try statement's depth: the IR's after the instruction before the handler (its body's jump or return),"] [1359 4 "// with the exception; the IR's depth there is the cleanup row's (an unreached instruction's is not known)"] [1380 1 "// calculateStackdepth is calculate_stackdepth."] [1428 2 "// SETUP_*'s jump to a handler no instruction is covered by (handlerDepths' setup-reached entries; queue 248)"] [1442 1 "// insertPrefix is insert_prefix_instructions."] [1458 62 "// 3.15: codegen_enter_scope's, bcEmit"] [1480 1 "// bcAddedExcept is the handler of an instruction basicblock_addop appends to b (queue 248): it never sets i_except, so"] [1481 1 "// the slot keeps what was there: a removed instruction's handler when the block shrank (Go's slice keeps it past the"] [1482 1 "// length, as the block's array does), else nothing (calloc's NULL). A handler's entry block (PUSH_EXC_INFO first) lost"] [1483 1 "// CPython's SETUP_CLEANUP, its last instruction shifted into the slot."] [1488 2 "// a slot Go's append never wrote is the zero instruction (op 0, CACHE: never one of the block's)"] [1495 1 "// normalizeJumps is normalize_jumps."] [1511 3 "// a new block's slots were never written: neither has a handler (cfg_builder_new_block, basicblock_addop)"] [1519 1 "// optimizeLoadFast is optimize_load_fast."] [1604 16 "// 3.15 pushes the instruction's own index"] [1607 43 "// PUSH_REF(i, NOT_LOCAL), the C's inner i"] [1621 5 "// 3.15: an opcode that consumes no inputs (the iterable stays the iterator's support)"] [1632 35 "// 3.15's END_SEND pops 3"] [1675 56 "// 3.15: BB_HAS_FALLTHROUGH, an empty block's too"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[57 18] [57 28] [67 18] [67 28] [78 19] [78 29] [111 21] [121 17] [125 18] [125 28] [137 14] [137 33] [152 45] [180 18] [180 28] [188 18] [188 28] [211 19] [211 26] [214 19] [214 29] [239 18] [239 28] [269 29] [330 69] [354 25] [369 23] [370 25] [386 6] [386 30] [445 18] [445 28] [459 19] [459 30] [498 22] [505 23] [510 7] [510 15] [543 30] [551 31] [563 23] [566 25] [605 37] [606 24] [626 23] [700 12] [700 29] [703 41] [704 26] [785 12] [785 29] [899 12] [899 29] [912 14] [912 33] [927 12] [927 24] [934 12] [934 23] [952 6] [952 20] [970 9] [970 29] [987 6] [987 14] [1001 28] [1001 39] [1002 42] [1011 18] [1011 25] [1012 38] [1032 18] [1032 28] [1048 18] [1048 28] [1094 22] [1107 19] [1107 29] [1132 18] [1132 31] [1136 18] [1136 28] [1161 18] [1161 28] [1194 17] [1199 22] [